    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABHa1BZQ",
      "title": "eth/079-080 + eth/085: OP Mainnet OPE key rotation (batcher, proposer, unsafe signer)",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1569,
      "body": "OP Mainnet OP Enterprise key rotation, same shape as the OP Sepolia tasks: eth/079 sets the OPE batcher and eth/085 the OPE unsafe block signer, both with `SetBatcherAndOrSigner` from the FoundationUpgradeSafe (already the OP Mainnet SystemConfig owner, so no owner override); eth/080 rotates the `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) proposer on the OP Mainnet DisputeGameFactory with `SetDisputeGameArgs`, signed by the L1PAO.\n\nNumbering follows the calendar dates: eth/079-080 on Nov 6 after Unichain eth/074-078 (#1564, which this PR is stacked on), eth/081 left free for U21 Mainnet (Nov 16), Soneium at eth/082-084 on Nov 19 (#1566, now stacked on this PR), and the signer at eth/085 on Nov 20. Pins: eth/079 FUS 77, eth/080 L1PAO 47 / FUS 78 / SC 74, eth/085 FUS 82 (after Soneium; U21 not accounted for yet, so U21 will move eth/082-085 pins and hashes).\n\nAll OPE addresses are `0xdead…dead` placeholders: batcher `…2001dead`, unsafe signer `…2002dead`, proposer `…2003dead`. `just simulate-stack` passes with the VALIDATION.md hashes on both signing paths (local runs needed retries on the public Unichain L2 RPC used by eth/074/077/078).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T21:13:24Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-30T20:51:27Z",
      "additions": 553,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM8AAAABLy3l9Q",
      "title": "Support ZK_DISPUTE_GAME (type 10) in SetDisputeGameArgs",
      "author": "Inphi",
      "number": 1597,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds game type 10 (`ZKDisputeGame`) to `SetDisputeGameArgs`, so a U22 chain can change its ZK game args (prestate, verifier, challenge and prove durations, challenger bond) through this template. The 140-byte layout follows `OPContractsManagerUtils.makeGameArgs`, and the bounds follow the OPCM StandardValidator ZK checks. As with types 5 and 9, the live impl is kept, because the ZK impl returns 0 from `gameType()`.\r\n\r\nThe new regression tests run against the `zk-proofs-2` Sepolia devnet, the only Sepolia chain with type 10 set. I ran them locally against a recent block. The earlier `SetDisputeGameArgs` tests need an archive RPC, so I could not run them locally; CI covers them.\r\n\r\nPart of https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/proofs-team/issues/7\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-30T15:06:57Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 243,
      "deletions": 16
    },
